Cactus Code Thorn SystemTopology
Author(s)    : Erik Schnetter <schnetter@gmail.com>
Maintainer(s): Erik Schnetter <schnetter@gmail.com>
Licence      : LGPL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

Report the MPI process/host mapping and the node hardware topology
(cores, PUs, caches, NUMA memory) as reported by MPI and hwloc.

Optionally bind OpenMP threads -- and their memory allocations -- to
specific processing units, automatically backing off if this process
is already confined to part of the node by a job scheduler, cgroup, or
launcher affinity setting. On heterogeneous (P-core/E-core) CPUs,
optionally restrict to performance cores only.

Expose the discovered topology to other thorns (e.g. Carpet/LoopControl,
Carpet/CarpetLib, CactusUtils/MemSpeed) via aliased functions
(GetNumSMTThreads, GetMaxSMTThreads, GetCacheInfo1, GetMPIProcessInfo),
which use it to make cache- and NUMA-aware tiling and allocation
decisions.

See doc/documentation.tex for details.
